CAT = "s66BrokerDealers"; SEG = "BDA"
Q = [
('A company sells its own new bonds directly to investors, without any firm. Under the USA the company is:',
 'Not a broker-dealer', ['Broker-dealer', 'Agent', 'Investment adviser'],
 'USA Section 401(c) excludes issuers from the broker-dealer definition, along with agents, banks and certain out-of-state firms. Its employees who sell may still be agents.'),
('A dealer that regularly quotes prices at which it will buy and sell a stock is a:',
 'Market maker', ['Transfer agent', 'Introducing broker', 'Clearing agent'],
 'The Exchange Act defines a market maker as a dealer that holds itself out as willing to buy and sell a security for its own account on a regular or continuous basis.'),
('Under the Securities Act of 1933, a firm that buys shares from an issuer to distribute them to the public is:',
 'Underwriter', ['Market maker', 'Transfer agent', 'Issuer'],
 'The 1933 Act defines an underwriter as anyone who purchases from an issuer with a view to distribution, or offers or sells for an issuer in connection with a distribution.'),
('Which broker-dealer employee is not an agent under the USA?',
 'Receptionist taking no orders', ['Salaried salesperson', 'Branch manager who also solicits', 'Part-time order taker'],
 'An agent is an individual who represents a broker-dealer in effecting or attempting to effect securities trades. Clerical staff who do not solicit or take orders are not agents; how a salesperson is paid does not matter.'),
('A broker-dealer applies for registration on:',
 'Form BD', ['Form ADV', 'Form U4', 'Form D'],
 'Form BD is the uniform application for broker-dealer registration with the SEC, SROs and states. Individuals use Form U4, and advisers use Form ADV.'),
('When the Administrator requires a surety bond of a broker-dealer, the USA says it must accept instead:',
 'Deposit of cash or securities', ['Letter from a major client', "Officer's personal guarantee", 'FINRA membership certificate'],
 'USA Section 202(f) requires the Administrator to accept an appropriate deposit of cash or securities in place of any required bond.'),
('Since NSMIA, a state may not require a registered broker-dealer to:',
 'Keep records beyond SEC rules', ['Pay a registration fee', 'Register its agents', 'Answer a fraud inquiry'],
 'NSMIA bars states from imposing capital, custody, margin, financial responsibility or books and records requirements that differ from or add to the federal rules. States keep registration and antifraud powers.'),
('Under the USA, an agent is an individual who represents:',
 'Broker-dealer or issuer', ['Investment adviser only', 'Any corporation', 'State Administrator'],
 "USA Section 401(b) defines an agent as an individual, other than a broker-dealer, who represents a broker-dealer or issuer in effecting or attempting to effect securities trades. Advisers' staff are IARs."),
("An employee sells her company's stock to fellow employees and gets no commission or bonus for it. Under the USA she is:",
 'Not an agent', ['Agent of the issuer', 'Broker-dealer', 'Investment adviser representative'],
 'USA Section 401(b) excludes an individual representing an issuer in transactions with its existing employees, partners or directors when no commission or other pay is given for soliciting.'),
('Under the USA, a bank that effects securities trades is:',
 'Excluded from the definition', ['Federal covered broker-dealer', 'Required to register in every state', 'Treated as an agent'],
 'Banks, savings institutions and trust companies are excluded from the USA definition of broker-dealer, though federal banking and securities laws still apply to them.'),
('A firm licensed in State A, with no office in State B, sells to an existing State A client who is visiting State B. In State B it:',
 'Need not register', ['Must register as a broker-dealer', 'Must make a notice filing', 'Must register its agent only'],
 'USA Section 401(c) excludes a firm with no place of business in the state that is licensed where it has an office and sells to an existing customer who is not a resident of the state.'),
('Under the USA, registering a broker-dealer automatically registers which of its people as agents?',
 'Partners, officers and directors', ['Every employee, clerical included', 'All branch office staff', 'No one at all'],
 'USA Section 202(a) states that registering a broker-dealer automatically registers as agents its partners, officers and directors, and persons in similar roles.'),
('If an applicant disclosed a final order before registering, the Administrator may base a revocation on it only within how long after registration?',
 '90 days', ['30 days', 'One year', 'Five years'],
 'USA Section 204(a) bars a revocation based solely on a final order the applicant disclosed before registration unless the proceeding starts within the next 90 days. This does not apply to renewals.'),
("A firm that executes a customer's order and charges a commission is acting as:",
 'Broker', ['Dealer', 'Principal', 'Underwriter'],
 'A broker acts as agent for the customer and earns a commission. A dealer acts as principal, trading from its own inventory and charging a markup or markdown.'),
('A Rule 10b-10 confirmation must disclose whether the firm acted:',
 'As agent or as principal', ['With or without a solicitation', "Under its own or a client's discretion", 'Through an exchange or in private'],
 'Rule 10b-10 requires the confirmation to state whether the broker-dealer acted as agent for the customer, for another person, for both, or as principal for its own account.'),
('Under the USA, every broker-dealer and agent registration expires:',
 'On December 31 unless renewed', ['One year after it was granted', 'Three years after it was granted', 'Only when revoked'],
 'USA Section 201(e) provides that every registration or notice filing expires on December 31 unless renewed, matching the CRD renewal cycle.'),
]
